{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"web_search","id":"exec-a5eca403-aba6-40ca-99d1-b5e01b3cab0b","query":"site:forum.intervals.icu oauth token refresh_token expires_in scope Duplicate scope Intervals.icu ...","action":{"type":"search","queries":["site:forum.intervals.icu oauth token refresh_token expires_in scope Duplicate scope Intervals.icu","site:intervals.icu oauth authorize api oauth token scopes"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search0","snippet":"# Oura sync issue — daily OAuth token refresh not working ... The data is visible in the Oura app but doesn’t appear in Intervals","title":"Oura sync issue — daily OAuth token refresh not working - Bug Reports - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/oura-sync-issue-daily-oauth-token-refresh-not-working/130138"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search1","snippet":"- Fixed connecting (or reconnecting) to intervals.icu failing with a “Duplicate scope CALENDAR” error — introduced in v3.0.1 alongside the new calendar push. ... Root","title":"Domestique - a free, open source, science based cycling training app - Page 3 - AI Tools - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/domestique-a-free-open-source-science-based-cycling-training-app/130388?page=3"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search2","snippet":"The MCP server at https://connect.icuvisor.app/mcp receives the request and is supposed to use your OAuth token to call the Intervals.icu API on your behalf ...","title":"Icuvisor.app - opensource local MCP server, shipped as a signed binary for Mac and Windows - AI Tools - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/icuvisor-app-opensource-local-mcp-server-shipped-as-a-signed-binary-for-mac-and-windows/130087"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search3","snippet":"`curl -X POST https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token \\ ... For each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access) and use commas to separate multiple scopes.","title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support - Announcements - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search4","snippet":"Integrate your app with Intervals.icu ... Maybe some settings in the web view are blocking network calls? ... Maybe I have missed it, but what","title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support - Page 3 - Announcements - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=3"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search5","snippet":"Since around July 18 my Suunto wellness data (sleep, HRV, resting HR) stopped arriving in Intervals.icu automatically. ... So the wellness checkbox is on, but","title":"Suunto wellness no longer syncs automatically - manual \"Download Old Data\" works - Bug Reports - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/suunto-wellness-no-longer-syncs-automatically-manual-download-old-data-works/130829"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search6","snippet":"Example using an access_token from OAuth (ACTIVITY:WRITE scope is required): ... You need to store the Intervals.icu athlete_id obtained via OAuth flow so you can","title":"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search7","snippet":"URL = https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=45&redirect_uri=intervalscompanion://oauth-callback&scope=... ... It sounds like it does not, as the login code tries to use the embedded browser ","title":"Intervals Companion v3 updates for Apple Health and workout syncing - External Projects - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-companion-v3-updates-for-apple-health-and-workout-syncing/124208"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search8","snippet":"New: DunMove now has an official OAuth API integration with Intervals.icu. * Connect once in the DunMove dashboard and all new plans and changes will","title":"DunMove – automatic training plan sync with Intervals.icu - External Projects - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/dunmove-automatic-training-plan-sync-with-intervals-icu/110654"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search9","snippet":"Duplicate Intervals.icu Activities Referencing Same Strava-linked Activity ... * Verify token string formatting (no extra spaces/characters). ... * Intervals.icu OAuth support ... What to do:","title":"Intervals.icu FAQ - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-faq/123707"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search10","snippet":"You sign in with Intervals.icu OAuth and paste one URL into Claude, ChatGPT, or Grok. IntervalSync never sees your API key; it holds a revocable","title":"Request for Official MCP Support for AI Tools (ChatGPT, Claude, ...) - Feature Requests - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/request-for-official-mcp-support-for-ai-tools-chatgpt-claude/126164"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"forum.intervals.icu","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"# (Yet Another) AI Coach - Montis.icu ... Best in a Web Browser (rather than Mobile app); Go to `Privacy Settings` ... Complete the OAUTH","title":"(Yet Another) AI Coach - Montis.icu - Page 17 - AI Tools - Intervals.icu Forum","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/yet-another-ai-coach-montis-icu/117856?page=17"}]}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"curl -L -s --max-time 20 'https://r.jina.ai/https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609' | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"Title: API access to Intervals.icu - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\n\nURL Source: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\n\nPublished Time: 2026-10-14T18:37:49+00:00\n\nMarkdown Content:\n## post by david on 14 Oct\n\nIntervals.icu now has a public API for other applications. To use it you need to generate an API key in /settings (look for “Developer Settings” near the bottom). Your API key allows other applications to access your Intervals.icu data. Be careful what you do with it! If you suspect that your key may have been compromised immediately clear or re-generate it.\n\nBy using the API you agree to the [Intervals.icu API Terms and Conditions](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-terms-and-conditions/114087) .\n\nPlease not that **data from Strava is not available from the API**. Their terms and conditions do not allow it.\n\nUpdate 9th October 2026: Garmin terms and conditions have been updated and **It is likely that we will have to block access to Garmin data via the API soon**.\n\nUpdate 14th October 2026: The revisions to the agreement are part of the planned reopening of the Garmin Connect Developer Program. **There will be an easier path for individuals and apps to access data from Garmin devices**.\n\nThe API uses [basic authentication](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basic_access_authentication) for personal use. **The username is “API_KEY” and the password your API key**. Example using curl:\n\n`$ curl -u API_KEY:1l0nlqjq3j1obdhg08rz5rfhx https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/2049151/activities.csv`\n\nApps intended to be used by more than one person should use [OAuth](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759) and Bearer tokens.\n\nI generated some API docs:\n\n*   [RapiDoc UI (best)](https://intervals.icu/api-docs.html)\n*   [Swagger UI (retro)](https://intervals.icu/api/v1/docs/swagger-ui/index.html)\n\nNote that you can use “0” for the athlete id for endpoints that accept an athlete id in the path. This will use the athlete for the API key or bearer token used to make the call.\n\nAlso you can [extend Intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/extending-intervals-icu/46565) itself using Javascript.\n\nThere are some guides for common API tasks:\n\n*   [Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-integration-cookbook/80090)\n*   [Uploading planned workouts to Intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/uploading-planned-workouts-to-intervals-icu/63624)\n\n## [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-rate-limits-1)Rate Limits\n\nThere are limits per day (reset at midnight UTC) and per rolling 15 minute window. The following http headers are returned on each request:\n\n```\nX-RateLimit-Limit: <15m limit>,<daily limit>\nX-RateLimit-Remaining: <15m limit remaining>,<daily limit remaining>\n```\n\nOver rate limit requests receive a 429 status code and a Retry-After http header indicating how many seconds need to elapse until the call might succeed.\n\n```\nRetry-After: 370\n```\n\nThere is an additional limit of 10 calls per second per IP address. This limit does not return any rate limit related http headers.\n\nRate limits are enforced differently for API key callers and OAuth client apps.\n\n### [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-oauth-client-apps-2)OAuth Client Apps\n\nThe default daily rate limit is 100/user per day up to 500 users (max 50000 requests), with a minimum of 5000. The daily limit resets at midnight UTC. Note that the per-user number is used to calculate the total daily limit and is not applied per-user, so backfills and new-user setup tasks should not be an issue.\n\nThe requests per 15 minute limit is 1/8 of the daily limit with a minimum of 2500. This is a rolling limit and does not reset at specific intervals.\n\nIf you have more than 500 users and need a higher daily limit, or a lower limit for safety, contact [support@intervals.icu](mailto:support@intervals.icu). The limits are to protect the Intervals.icu infrastructure from apps with many users suddenly generating many more calls than usual.\n\nCurrent limits and API usage information can be found on the oauth client management page (look for “Manage App” on your app on /settings/apps).\n\n### [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-api-key-callers-3)API Key Callers\n\nAPI key calls are limited to 5000 requests per day and 2500 requests per rolling 15 minute window. If you need more than that you need to create an app using [OAuth](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759).\n\n## [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-cloudflare-note-4)Cloudflare Note\n\nIntervals.icu uses Cloudflare and CF considers requests from some client libraries (e.g. `Python-urllib`) to be suspicious and maybe challenge or block them. The easy fix is to change the user agent to look like a browser.\n\nread  113 min\n\n## post by Andrii_Magalich on Apr 2, 2020\n\n## post by david on Apr 3, 2020\n\n10 days later\n\n## post by david on Apr 13, 2020\n\n29 days later\n\n## post by Jules_Cusson-Fradet on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by david on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by Jules_Cusson-Fradet on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by david on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by Jules_Cusson-Fradet on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by david on May 14, 2020\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
